  <!-- ─── This is real (live gateway evidence) ───────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="this-is-real">
    <span class="section-eyebrow" data-reveal>⬛ This is real</span>
    <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:60ms">Not a mockup. A running gateway.</h2>
    <p class="section-sub" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
      These are real responses from a live FoundryGate gateway, captured during
      testing on September 1, 2026. This is exactly what a developer's tools see.
    </p>

    <div class="proof-grid">

      <div class="proof-card" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:0ms">
        <div class="proof-head">
          <span class="proof-dot proof-dot--green"></span>
          <span class="proof-title">A normal request</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="proof-body"><span class="st-ok">HTTP/1.1 200 OK</span>
<span class="hdr">x-fg-remaining-quota</span>: 97668
<span class="hdr">x-fg-remaining-tpm</span>: 19984
<span class="hdr">x-fg-tokens-consumed</span>: 16</pre>
        <div class="proof-caption">
          Every answer comes back with a live meter reading: this request used
          16 tokens, and 97,668 remain in this developer's monthly budget.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proof-card" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:80ms">
        <div class="proof-head">
          <span class="proof-dot proof-dot--amber"></span>
          <span class="proof-title">Going too fast</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="proof-body"><span class="st-warn">HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests</span>
<span class="hdr">Retry-After</span>: 50</pre>
        <div class="proof-caption">
          Burning through tokens too quickly? The gateway says "wait 50 seconds."
          Coding tools understand this and slow down on their own.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proof-card" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:160ms">
        <div class="proof-head">
          <span class="proof-dot proof-dot--red"></span>
          <span class="proof-title">Monthly budget spent</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="proof-body"><span class="st-err">HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden</span>

&#123;
  <span class="hdr">"statusCode"</span>: 403,
  <span class="hdr">"message"</span>: "Token quota is exceeded.
    Try again in 29 days, 9 hours,
    50 minutes, and 5 seconds."
&#125;</pre>
        <div class="proof-caption">
          What a developer sees when their monthly budget runs out — the very
          same second it runs out. It even says exactly when it comes back.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proof-card" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:240ms">
        <div class="proof-head">
          <span class="proof-dot proof-dot--blue"></span>
          <span class="proof-title">A real AI assistant, through the gateway</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="proof-body"><span class="dim">$</span> codex exec "Reply with exactly: pong"
<span class="out">pong</span>
<span class="dim">tokens used: 9,139</span></pre>
        <div class="proof-caption">
          A real coding assistant (Codex CLI) answering through the gateway —
          9,139 tokens counted against its owner's budget, like every other request.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p class="proof-note">
      Captured from a live FoundryGate gateway on 2026-09-01. Header names and timings are unedited.
    </p>
